< \paragraph{The trace already holds the right bid.}
< The verifier recovers 81--100\% of the gap at 768 tokens with no extra tokens, and 80--100\% across parser tolerances of 1--5\% (Table~\ref{tab:main}); built from the annotators' labels instead of the parser on the 150 annotated traces it scores 0.963, against 0.959 from the parser and 0.897 for the model's answer. It helps only once most options are evaluated: at 256 tokens it lowers $q$ by 0.002--0.046 (Figure~\ref{fig:main}c). The stricter $K-1$ variant never lowers $q$ by more than 0.001 at any budget and recovers 77--96\% at 768 tokens. Sampling is no substitute for length: two 384-token samples with majority voting score 0.06--0.18 below one 768-token sample at the same token count.
